language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Find a 10 digit number that uses each digit 0 to 9 exactly once, where the number formed by its first n digits is divisible by n.
find digit : matrix indexed by [int(1..10)] of int(0..9)
find number : int(0..9999999999)

branching on [digit]

such that
$ the number uses each of the digits 0 to 9 exactly once
allDiff(digit),
$ the number is read from its digits from left to right
number = (sum k : int(1..10) . digit[k] * 10**(10-k)),
$ the number formed by the first n digits is divisible by n, for n from 1 to 10
forAll n : int(1..10) . ((sum k : int(1..n) . digit[k] * 10**(n-k)) % n) = 0
